---
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<section id="start" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="start-title">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="start-title">Try it in 5 minutes</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      You need Docker (running) and bash. No API keys, no Rust toolchain and no Nextflow install.
      The demo replays recorded model answers, so no model is called.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="split">
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="step-label">1. Run the demo</p>
      <pre class="command" tabindex="0"><code>git clone https://github.com/pingedbrain/nf-agents.git && cd nf-agents && demo/run.sh</code></pre>
      <p class="muted small">
        The script runs one pipeline with an agent step twice, with <code>--greeting hello</code>
        and then <code>--greeting bonjour</code>. It then asks the lineage server what changed.
        The first run builds both images (about 3 minutes); later runs take about 24 seconds.
      </p>
      <p class="step-label">2. Ask Claude Code about the runs</p>
      <pre class="command" tabindex="0"><code>claude mcp add --transport stdio nf-lineage -- docker run -i --rm --network none -v "$PWD/demo/.run:/demo:ro" nf-lineage-mcp:demo --store /demo/.lineage</code></pre>
      <p class="muted small">
        The server is read-only and has no network access. Ask "What changed between my last two
        runs?" The full transcript and troubleshooting are in <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}docs/`}>the docs</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Terminal title="demo/run.sh output, abridged" note="synthetic data, research use only">
{`1. list_runs: run A agitated_raman (lid://b39e82b0…), run B agitated_gilbert (lid://2385fd14…)
2. diff A -> B: params.greeting: "hello" → "bonjour" (nothing else changed)
3. AI step QC_NOTE: model openai/gpt-5-mini, answer "no" (confidence 0.9) to "any lowercase letters?"
4. provenance of run B summary.txt: SUMMARIZE ← TRANSFORM ← GENERATE ← seed.txt
5. check run A summary.txt: Valid (/demo/results-hello/summary.txt)
6. check again after appending a line to it: Mismatch (the file no longer matches its lineage)
tour passed: 6/6 answers as expected`}
    </Terminal>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .split {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .split > * {
    flex: 1 1 320px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .step-label {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .command {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    background: #121614;
    color: #dde3df;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .command code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', ui-monospace, monospace;
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .stack code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.875em;
  }
</style>
